Liturgical Sermons: rights and licences

This repository contains material of four kinds, under different terms.

1. Historical editions. The sermons are transcribed from printed editions that
   are in the public domain in the United States. Each edition is cited on the
   Texts & Licences page of the site and in catalog.json.

2. Digitized copies. The page images of those editions are held by the libraries
   and archives named with each sermon. This repository does not contain or
   redistribute the page images; any use of them is governed by the institution
   that holds them.

3. Translations, introductions and notes. The English translations, editorial
   introductions, topics, Scripture references and editorial notes prepared for
   Liturgical Sermons are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International licence (CC BY 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   Text generated wholly by AI may not be protected by copyright in the United
   States; the licence applies to whatever rights exist in this material.
   Suggested attribution: "Translation from Liturgical Sermons
   (https://financeprofessormckee.github.io/Liturgical-Sermons/), licensed under
   CC BY 4.0."

4. Software. The HTML templates, stylesheets, scripts and tools are released
   under the MIT License, below.

